WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.420
After another huge brawl and face-off, the
ending of Cobra Kai Season 5 leaves the future

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:11.690
of John Kreese's karate dojo in enormous doubt
and perhaps signals the imminent end of the

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:12.690
series itself.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:17.320
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining how Cobra Kai's

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:22.590
fifth season could be setting up a big twist
in Season 6, plus I'll be revealing the little

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:26.349
details and easter eggs you might have missed
in the season 5 finale.

00:00:26.349 --> 00:00:29.159
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:29.159 --> 00:00:34.110
Season 5 ends with a smashing show-down as
Daniel triumphs over Silver, crane-kicking

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.140
him through a giant glass cobra.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:41.730
As Silver's students line up to quit and throw
off their Cobra Kai shirts in disgust after

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:46.650
the revelation their sensei bribed the referee
at the All Valley Tournament in Season 4,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:50.080
it appears that Cobra Kai's days may truly
be numbered.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:55.010
Interestingly, Daniel defeats the sneaky sensei
by employing against him the Quick Silver

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.960
rules that Silver taught him in Karate Kid
3.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:02.240
This is exactly what Chozen recommended to
Daniel in the very first episode.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:05.229
To catch serpent, you must think like serpent.

00:01:05.229 --> 00:01:07.399
We will use his style against him.

00:01:07.399 --> 00:01:11.859
Daniel's victory here shows he's been willing
to embrace other karate styles in addition

00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:16.210
to those he learned from Mr Miyagi, something
he admitted to Johnny at the end of Season

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:20.170
4 when he saw his own daughter using some
of Eagle Fang's moves at the tournament.

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:23.819
I see some of what you teach can be good sometimes.

00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:29.299
This continues the overarching Cobra Kai series
theme of former foes reconciling and then

00:01:29.299 --> 00:01:34.680
making something new by blending their contrasting
attitudes and styles of karate together,

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.580
We've combined our different styles to train
our students into the best fighters I've ever

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:39.580
seen.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.619
By the way, notice that how Daniel lands his
final blow on Silver by crane-kicking him

00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:48.170
into the glass cobra on the wall behind him
is a call-back to when Silver fell into a

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:53.270
pane of glass during his fight with Mr Miyagi
in The Karate Kid 3, as well as to Daniel's

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:58.119
winning kick to take out the young Cobra Kai
star Johnny in the original movie.

00:01:58.119 --> 00:02:03.240
But let's not forget the crucial part the
Miyagi-Do students also played in taking down

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.240
Silver.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.509
After uncovering the incriminating footage
of Tory's talk with her sensei, they remembered

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:13.819
Chozen's training and advice to work together
as a team against the onslaught of Cobra Kai.

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:15.660
He said that the snakes will take us down
one by one.

00:02:15.660 --> 00:02:16.890
But what if we weren't a bunch of ones?

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:18.579
The only way we win is if we work together.

00:02:18.579 --> 00:02:23.680
Similar to how, together, they surrounded
the basket of eggs to protect it against Chozen,

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.209
they formed a barrier around Anthony and the
tablet which was uploading the incriminating

00:02:28.209 --> 00:02:29.530
clip of Silver.

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:34.700
So, by the end of Season 5, with the exception
of Kreese – more on him shortly – the

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:39.760
biggest Cobra Kai and Miyagi-Do rivalries
appear to have been resolved for both the

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.430
OG Karate Kid characters and the new generation.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:47.270
Miguel and Robbie are now friends;
Sam and Tory are reconciled and fought together

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:51.500
against Sensei Kim, with Devon also abandoning
Cobra Kai to join them;

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.780
Oh, I will be a champion.

00:02:52.780 --> 00:02:54.500
But I'll get there my way, not yours.

00:02:54.500 --> 00:02:58.220
meanwhile Kenny's beef with Robbie seems to
have been put aside;

00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.920
and even Stingray redeems himself when he
comes to rescue Daniel.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:02.920
What are you doing?

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:04.209
It's pitch black out.

00:03:04.209 --> 00:03:05.709
Stingrays see better in the dark.

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:10.340
But with Silver hauled off by the police,
what's left now for the series and the Cobra

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.000
Kai legacy he repeatedly spoke about in Season
5?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.310
I never had any children.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.450
My only legacy is Cobra Kai.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:22.901
Well, conveniently in Season 5 we're introduced
to the granddaughter of Master Kim, who Silver

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:26.220
invited over from Korea to join him at Cobra
Kai.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:28.140
I did not get on the plane for money.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.480
What I'm offering you is legacy.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:35.409
Your grandfather didn't teach American soldiers
the Way of the Fist just to use on the battlefield.

00:03:35.409 --> 00:03:38.270
We have to share his style with the world.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:43.621
As a child, she avidly watched the young Kreese
and Silver train with her grandfather, and

00:03:43.621 --> 00:03:48.540
she's clearly motivated to make her own mark
in the martial arts world now.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:52.950
Silver may be arrested, but Cobra Kai as a
dojo was already accepted to compete at the

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:58.749
Sekai Taikai international tournament, and
if she wanted she could recruit her own students,

00:03:58.749 --> 00:04:03.189
perhaps from Korea, and enter the competition
under the Cobra Kai name, thus continuing

00:04:03.189 --> 00:04:06.959
the legacy of Cobra Kai, fulfilling what Silver
predicted:

00:04:06.959 --> 00:04:08.640
Cobra Kai will go on forever.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.870
Though, of course, it's also possible that
she'd want to distance herself from the bad

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:15.780
publicity surrounding Silver and his dojo.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:21.079
The Sekai Taikai tournament will undoubtedly
be the focus of Season 6, and it seems more

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:25.550
than likely that Sensei Kim will be competing
there in some form or another bringing her

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:30.430
grandfather's "Way of the Fist" style of fighting
to the competition, and setting up a clash

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:35.250
with the karate styles championed by Daniel
and Johnny at Miyagi-Do and Eagle Fang.

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:40.710
Chozen also revealed that his uncle Sato,
the secondary villain from Karate Kid 2, had

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.860
major beef with Master Kim and I expect a
lot of that history will be revealed in Season

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:49.720
6, setting up a collision between Chozen and
Sensei Kim.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:52.270
My uncle Sato did not speak much of Kim Sun-Yung.

00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:53.970
But I know he had much anger towards him.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:59.970
Chozen also revealed that Master Kim's teachings
are behind a lot of Cobra Kai's brutal philosophy.

00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:03.080
Kim Sun-Yung's style is based on deception.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.080
No honor.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.080
No mercy.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:08.810
Of course, John Kreese, the OG big bad of
the original Karate Kid film, will be back

00:05:08.810 --> 00:05:13.500
to mix things up in Season 6 after faking
his own death yet again.

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.930
The finale began with Kreese pretending he
was done with everything after being tricked

00:05:17.930 --> 00:05:23.350
by his former star student Johnny and arch
enemy Daniel, and telling Tory to look after

00:05:23.350 --> 00:05:25.810
herself from now on and forget about him.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.449
And his opening words in the final episode…

00:05:28.449 --> 00:05:29.449
This is it.

00:05:29.449 --> 00:05:30.449
End of the line.

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:34.540
…are a call-back to what Danny's mum said
to her teen son when they first arrived in

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:38.480
LA, the event that kicked off the whole Karate
Kid and Cobra Kai saga.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:39.480
This is it.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.580
This is the end of the line.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:45.860
That's a clever little signal that although
Kreese claims he's giving up, this moment

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:50.900
is really just the beginning of a new chapter
in his life, just like it was for Daniel all

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:52.099
those years ago.

00:05:52.099 --> 00:05:56.539
Now that an unrepentant Kreese has broken
out of prison, it'll be interesting to see

00:05:56.539 --> 00:06:01.569
how he reacts to Silver's arrest and discovering
that the students from his beloved dojo have

00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:02.730
abandoned it.

00:06:02.730 --> 00:06:06.930
The threat that Johnny made to wipe out Kreese's
legacy appears to have come true.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.370
You wanna know why I'm in this fight?

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:10.120
So I can erase everything you did.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.889
And every mark you left.

00:06:11.889 --> 00:06:12.889
Every memory of you.

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:17.710
I expect Kreese might well team up with Sensei
Kim when he discovers she's been at Cobra

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:18.870
Kai.

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:22.330
Remember from the flashback that they both
seemed to get along with each other when they

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:27.560
were younger, and this will be Kreese's opportunity
to re-establish the legacy of Cobra Kai which,

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:30.319
of course, came from Kim's grandfather.

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:34.780
On top of that, going up against Daniel and
Johnny at the international tournament will

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:39.080
be a chance for him to get revenge on them
for the trick they pulled on him in prison.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:44.069
I think Kreese will also be looking to get
his own personal payback on Silver for framing

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:45.330
him for beating up Stingray.

00:06:45.330 --> 00:06:50.349
First of all, I'm not entirely convinced Silver
will be going to jail.

00:06:50.349 --> 00:06:54.909
He's got plenty of money to pay the best lawyers
around, and they could probably convince a

00:06:54.909 --> 00:07:00.680
jury that Stingray's new testimony is unreliable
given he already lied about Kreese.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:05.430
Plus, the video evidence of Silver beating
up Stingray has already been deleted.

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:10.099
If Silver does go free then, Kreese will likely
want his own revenge.

00:07:10.099 --> 00:07:12.259
There is an endgame, kid.

00:07:12.259 --> 00:07:13.259
Silver's going down.

00:07:13.259 --> 00:07:14.790
Only he doesn't know it yet.

00:07:14.790 --> 00:07:20.199
Now, Season 6 hasn't been confirmed by Netflix
yet, but apparently some scenes have already

00:07:20.199 --> 00:07:22.960
been filmed;
however, my feeling is that it could well

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.460
be the final season of the series.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:29.990
Many major character arcs have already been
wrapped up in Season 5, and it's hard to see

00:07:29.990 --> 00:07:35.000
how exactly the series could carry on and
top the stakes of the biggest karate tournament

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.000
in the world.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:40.919
It also makes me wonder whether there could
be a big surprise twist for the final season,

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:46.080
and I think there's a clue in the Season 5
moment when Daniel and Johnny were accepted

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.389
into the tournament and were asked for the
name of their dojo…

00:07:49.389 --> 00:07:51.430
We just need your dojo's name.

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.439
We are Miyagi-Do.

00:07:52.439 --> 00:07:54.259
And we are Eagle Fang.

00:07:54.259 --> 00:07:55.659
Well, which is it?

00:07:55.659 --> 00:08:00.900
Now, wild and out-there theory time, folks,
but what if Johnny and Daniel decide they

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:06.889
want to finally rehabilitate Cobra Kai by
taking on the mantle themselves, so that Miyagi-Do

00:08:06.889 --> 00:08:12.780
and Eagle Fang combine to become the new Cobra
Kai, or Miyagi-Cobra-Fang?

00:08:12.780 --> 00:08:17.710
It was Johnny after all who resurrected Cobra
Kai, and it would be an intriguing turn of

00:08:17.710 --> 00:08:23.020
events for the OG Karate Kid to rehabilitate
the dojo of his former nemesis.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:27.449
He did already of course train at Silver's
Cobra Kai in the third movie, and used some

00:08:27.449 --> 00:08:30.419
of those techniques this season to defeat
Silver.

00:08:30.419 --> 00:08:34.789
The biggest problem with this idea is that
it may be hard for Daniel to justify it as

00:08:34.789 --> 00:08:37.950
fitting in with and honouring Mr Miyagi's
legacy.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:42.390
Of course, the whole name thing may just be
a bit of fun and a meta moment alluding to

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:47.510
how fans have referred to Daniel and Johnny's
team up in earlier seasons as "Miyagi-Fang",

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:50.600
something also acknowledged by Stingray when
he gets ambushed.

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:51.600
Miyagi-Fangs?

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:56.740
Overall, I feel that Season 6 might be the
best way to end the Cobra Kai series on a

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:01.500
relatively high note, rather than dragging
things out for many more seasons.

00:09:01.500 --> 00:09:02.740
So, what do you think?

00:09:02.740 --> 00:09:07.120
Did you enjoy Season 5 and do you think the
series is ready to wrap things up for good

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.600
in Season 6?

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:13.130
You can tap here for more Cobra Kai videos
with easter eggs and details you missed.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:16.820
And if you liked this video, do leave a thumbs-up,
I really appreciate it.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:21.280
Thanks for enjoying Cobra Kai with me and
hope you have a marvellous movie-loving week!

00:09:21.280 --> 00:09:22.670
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

